  "proved": [
    "Rational coefficient extraction commutes with sums and scaling, and only empty/singleton factors contribute to a product singleton.",
    "Point-supported terms have zero coefficient at any monomial of a different full curve class.",
    "Only (0,beta) and (beta,0) contribute to the original singleton at a separating genus-zero gluing in positive class.",
    "Positive-class primary components contribute their dimension-checked signed divisor product; zero-class primary components contribute their dimension-checked classical cubic.",
    "A degree-zero primary vertex contributes zero unless its arity is three, so placements with larger arity on both original vertices have zero coefficient.",
    "The recursive coefficient evaluator is equal to the complete original expansion at every positive class and arbitrary marking count.",
    "The WDVV coefficient computed by this evaluator retains the original request, channel weights and all marking multiplicities."
  ],
